## A Geometry Homework Helper

Geometry is full of formulas — each one maps perfectly to a function.

### Rectangles

```xiom
fn area_of_rectangle(width: Float64, height: Float64) -> Float64 {
  return width * height;
}

fn perimeter_of_rectangle(width: Float64, height: Float64) -> Float64 {
  return 2.0 * (width + height);
}

fn main() -> Int {
  io.println(area_of_rectangle(5.0, 3.0));       // 15.0
  io.println(perimeter_of_rectangle(5.0, 3.0));  // 16.0
  return 0;
}
```

### Circles

```xiom
fn area_of_circle(radius: Float64) -> Float64 {
  return 3.14159 * radius * radius;
}

fn circumference_of_circle(radius: Float64) -> Float64 {
  return 2.0 * 3.14159 * radius;
}

fn main() -> Int {
  io.println(area_of_circle(3.0));          // ~28.27
  io.println(circumference_of_circle(3.0)); // ~18.85
  return 0;
}
```

### Triangles

```xiom
fn area_of_triangle(base: Float64, height: Float64) -> Float64 {
  return 0.5 * base * height;
}

fn main() -> Int {
  io.println(area_of_triangle(6.0, 4.0));  // 12.0
  return 0;
}
```

### A Shape Analyzer

```xiom
fn analyze_rectangle(width: Float64, height: Float64) {
  io.println("Rectangle " + "x: ");
  io.println(width);
  io.println(height);
  io.println("Area: ");
  io.println(area_of_rectangle(width, height));
  io.println("Perimeter: ");
  io.println(perimeter_of_rectangle(width, height));
}

fn main() -> Int {
  analyze_rectangle(4.0, 7.0);
  return 0;
}
```

Now you have a reusable math toolkit — never calculate by hand again!

